    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.notify\n\n### Question\n\nwhat am i doing wrong here, i am using lazy.nvim as a package manager and want to use mini notify :) I have done this and it works for LSP info but whenever i do something like :lua vim.notify('error', vim.log.levels.ERROR) it is showing in the command panel still and not as a notification, I am sure I have set something up wrong here. I was hoping to use this as a wrapper for all notifications.\r\n\r\nThanks in advance! :) \r\n\r\n```\r\nreturn {\r\n\t\"echasnovski/mini.notify\",\r\n\tconfig = function()\r\n\t\trequire(\"mini.notify\").setup({\r\n\t\t\twindow = {\r\n\t\t\t\tconfig = { border = \"rounded\" },\r\n\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t})\r\n\tend,\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.notify</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">what am i doing wrong here, i am using lazy.nvim as a package manager and want to use mini notify :) I have done this and it works for LSP info but whenever i do something like :lua vim.notify('error', vim.log.levels.ERROR) it is showing in the command panel still and not as a notification, I am sure I have set something up wrong here. I was hoping to use this as a wrapper for all notifications.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks in advance! :)</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"return {\n\t&quot;echasnovski/mini.notify&quot;,\n\tconfig = function()\n\t\trequire(&quot;mini.notify&quot;).setup({\n\t\t\twindow = {\n\t\t\t\tconfig = { border = &quot;rounded&quot; },\n\t\t\t},\n\t\t})\n\tend,\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">return {\n\t\"echasnovski/mini.notify\",\n\tconfig = function()\n\t\trequire(\"mini.notify\").setup({\n\t\t\twindow = {\n\t\t\t\tconfig = { border = \"rounded\" },\n\t\t\t},\n\t\t})\n\tend,\n}\n</code></pre></div>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.notify\nQuestion\nwhat am i doing wrong here, i am using lazy.nvim as a package manager and want to use mini notify :) I have done this and it works for LSP info but whenever i do something like :lua vim.notify('error', vim.log.levels.ERROR) it is showing in the command panel still and not as a notification, I am sure I have set something up wrong here. I was hoping to use this as a wrapper for all notifications.\nThanks in advance! :)\nreturn {\n\t\"echasnovski/mini.notify\",\n\tconfig = function()\n\t\trequire(\"mini.notify\").setup({\n\t\t\twindow = {\n\t\t\t\tconfig = { border = \"rounded\" },\n\t\t\t},\n\t\t})\n\tend,\n}",
